      "writtenOn": "2021-03-18T07:54:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I try to use \"chipset_in_or_transitionin_to_state(CHIPSET_STATE_ON)\" in lightbar_states(), it still get failure result.\n\nlightbar_states is pushed into HOOK_TICK.\nFrom the below log, it\u0027s late to update power state.\nSo, it may blink a while when plug in AC. Is there any other option to fix this problem? Or, it could add some flag when trigger HOOK_AC_CHANGE but it may not straightforward.\n\n\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\n21-03-18 14:18:17.564 [81.749103 CL: p1 s0 i500 v20000]\n21-03-18 14:18:17.567 [81.749906 AC on]\n21-03-18 14:18:17.572 [81.750349 event set 0x0000000000000008]\n21-03-18 14:18:17.574 [81.753996 power state 4 \u003d S0ix, in 0x007f]\n21-03-18 14:18:17.578 [81.755650 Release SLP_S3_L]\n21-03-18 14:18:17.581 [81.756145 Pass thru GPIO_DSW_PWROK: 1]\n[81.780604 chipset_in_or_transitioning_to_state(CHIPSET_STATE_ON) \u003d 0x0, SLP_S3:1;SLP_S0:1.]\n^^^^^^^^\nHere is problem that lightbar blink a while because power state is late to update.\n[81.794101 event clear B 0x0000000000000008]\n[81.807507 event clear 0x0000000000000008]\n21-03-18 14:18:17.622 [81.807826 ACPI query \u003d 4]\n[81.819261 event set 0x0000000008000000]\n21-03-18 14:18:17.635 [81.819962 event clear 0x0000000008000000]\n21-03-18 14:18:17.637 [81.820363 ACPI query \u003d 28]\nRTC: 0x0005c0f3 (377075.00 s)\n21-03-18 14:18:17.662 [81.853835 power state 11 \u003d S0ix-\u003eS0, in 0x007f]\n21-03-18 14:18:17.669 [81.855471 Release SLP_S3_L]\n21-03-18 14:18:17.669 [81.856631 Pass thru GPIO_DSW_PWROK: 1]\nRTC: 0x0005c0f3 (377075.00 s)\n21-03-18 14:18:17.731 [81.919690 power state 3 \u003d S0, in 0x007f]\n21-03-18 14:18:17.733 [81.921272 Release SLP_S3_L]\n21-03-18 14:18:17.737 [81.921845 Pass thru GPIO_DSW_PWROK: 1]\n[81.983378 C1: PE_SNK_Ready]\n21-03-18 14:18:17.793 [81.984331 C1: PE_VDM_Response]\n21-03-18 14:18:17.796 [81.986788 Ramp reset[81.988672 C1: PE_SNK_Ready]\n[81.989149 C1: PE_SNK_Select_Capability]\n\n\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d",
